HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uunniiffddeeff command appeared in 2.9BSD.  ANSI C support was added in
     FreeBSD 4.7.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The original implementation was written by Dave Yost <_D_a_v_e_@_Y_o_s_t_._c_o_m>.
     Tony Finch <_d_o_t_@_d_o_t_a_t_._a_t> rewrote it to support ANSI C.

BBUUGGSS
     ••   Expression evaluation is very limited.

     ••   Character constants are not evaluated.  String literals and character
         constants in --ff definition files are ignored rather than parsed as
         part of a macro's replacement tokens.

     ••   Only the basic form of C++ raw string literals is recognized, like
         R"(string)" without delimiters as in R"delimiter(string)delimiter".

     ••   Source files are processed one line at a time, so preprocessor direc‐
         tives split across more than one physical line (because of comments
         or backslash-newline) cannot be handled in every situation.

     ••   Trigraphs are not recognized.

     ••   There is no support for macros with different definitions at differ‐
         ent points in the source file.

     ••   The text-mode and ignore functionality does not correspond to modern
         cpp(1) behaviour.

